&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 1&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49923417</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 15:58:14 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: TrueScribe – Linux local AI transcription studio</title><link>https://truescribe.app/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Switched to Fedora a year ago. And because I needed to transcribe interviews offline from time to time, I was looking for something like MacWhisper for Linux. When I couldn't find one, I decided to build one. Because in this day and age, why the hell not! And yes, AI coding-agents were used.&lt;p&gt;I work as a .NET Software Engineer and I despise Electron Apps, so I decided to go with a semi-native Stack, consisting of C# and Avalonia.Net (hardware accelerated trough SkiaSharp) for the frontend and C++ for low-level model bindings (CTranslate2 for translation, Nemotron 3 NeMo-Speech.cpp for Speaker Identification via JSON-RPC worker).&lt;p&gt;A friend liked the app and told me to go Freemium, so here we are. Works also on Windows btw.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
